From: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: select split-PHY firmware for Cambium X7-35X

The Cambium X7-35X wires its QCN9224 as a split-PHY device for
simultaneous 5 and 6 GHz; the OEM firmware reports two PCI PHYs and
selects hardware mode 5. The stock firmware bundle contains both AMSS
variants, but the OTP-based selection starts the single-PHY variant on
this board.

Select the existing dual-MAC image for this machine and QCN9274 hw2.0
only. Firmware capability negotiation, calibration and regulatory
handling are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <linux/msi.h>
 #include <linux/pci.h>
 #include <linux/firmware.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 
 #include "core.h"
 #include "debug.h"
@@ -218,6 +219,13 @@ int ath12k_mhi_register(struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci)
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* X7-35X wires the split-PHY device for simultaneous 5/6 GHz.
+	 * Its OEM boot exposes two PHYs; OTP alone selects single-MAC.
+	 */
+	if (ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_QCN9274_HW20 &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("cambiumnetworks,x7-35x"))
+		dualmac = true;
+
 	if (dualmac) {
 		if (ab->fw.amss_dualmac_data && ab->fw.amss_dualmac_len > 0) {
 			/* use MHI firmware file from firmware-N.bin */
